          <h2 class="underline">The research</h2>
          <h3>Your rights as a research subject</h3>
          <p>By participating in this research, you are not entering into any kind of agreement, restriction or legally-binding contract.</p>
          <h3>Data collection</h3>
          <h4>How data will be collected</h4>
          <p>Usage data will be collected and stored in a local database during use. Data collection - or the application itself (potentially) - won&apos;t work without a database installed and database credentials setup in the app (server.js). (NOT IMPLEMENTED)</p>
          <h3>Withdrawal</h3>
          <h4>Your right to withdrawal</h4>
          <p>You may withdraw from the research at any time with no consequence or advance notice. If you wish to withdraw, please contact the researcher and let them know.</p>
          <h4>How will your data be used if you decide to withdraw?</h4>
          <p>If you wish to share the data which has been collected during your usage, you should send the researcher the exported data from your local database.</p>

          <hr />

          <h2 class="underline">Legal, Social, and Ethical Diclaimers</h2>
          <p>"Artificial Intelligence" refers to a field of machine learning, particularly concerning deep-learning and the emergence of Large Language Models (LLMs) and Generative Pre-trained Transformers (GPTs), it may be referred to in place of Large Language Models or Generative Pre-trained Transformers.</p>
          <br />

          <ul>
            <li>&bull;Artificial Intelligence should only be used according to global and local legislation regarding the usage of Artificial Intelligence.</li>
            <li>&bull;The output of Artificial Intelligence can be biased, or be manipulated by the user, server, or GPT/LLM provider (OpenAI).</li>
            <li>&bull;Artificial Intelligence is subject to the same censorship as information found on the web, with few exceptions.</li>
            <li>&bull;Any unconfirmed information from the usage of Artificial Intelligence is not legally-binding or admissible. This includes, but is not limited to: Global/Local laws & legislation, legal case studies, or other legal information</li>
            <li>&bull;Any harm that does occur due to the innapropriate/negligent use of Artificial Intelligence leading to harm is not legally admissible.</li>

            <li style="padding-top: 1rem;">Artificial Intelligence should not be used:</li>
            <li>&bull;to seek legal advice.</li>
            <li>&bull;to seek medical advice or treatment.</li>
            <li>&bull;to seek advice for poor mental health, mental illnesses, or other adverse mental conditions.</li>
            <li>&bull;for advice or guidance on any activity with any potential for harm of any kind.</li>
            <li>&bull;as a substitute for logical and critical evaluation of content.</li>
            <li>&bull;as a replacement for human interaction.</li>
          </ul>

